1
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:11,933
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,633 --> 00:00:41,267
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:42,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:46,767
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:55,433 --> 00:00:56,800
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,400
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,667
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,100
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:07,267
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,133 --> 00:01:11,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:17,000
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,167 --> 00:01:19,200
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:21,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:24,800
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,233 --> 00:01:28,300
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,367 --> 00:01:34,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,300
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:38,933
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:40,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,867 --> 00:01:47,400
<i> Looks like it's my lucky day.</i>

24
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:48,833
<i>It means I'm going to land
a job.</i>

25
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,000
<i> What? We look like thugs?</i>

26
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:51,533
<i>You sell, and I'll break
your head!</i>

27
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,667
<i>- Tough guys behind a screen!
- Come over here!</i>

28
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:54,967
<i> Miss Betchay's right again.</i>

29
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:56,833
<i>We'd really end up working
at the market.</i>

30
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,300
<i> Thief! Thief!</i>

31
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,300
<i>You're stealing from people
here at the market now, huh?</i>

32
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,300
<i>You choose. Get beaten up
or tell the truth?</i>

33
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,733
<i>Oh, wait. There's something
in my pocket.</i>

34
00:02:03,867 --> 00:02:05,700
<i> I found this earlier, Gabo.</i>

35
00:02:05,867 --> 00:02:07,633
<i> If you show up here again...</i>

36
00:02:07,733 --> 00:02:09,667
<i> I'll break your faces.</i>

37
00:02:09,767 --> 00:02:10,667
<i> Is that clear?!</i>

38
00:02:10,767 --> 00:02:13,000
- [KICKS LANDING]
- [CROWD CHEERING]

39
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:15,033
<i>- Run!
- Go, run!</i>

40
00:02:15,233 --> 00:02:16,500
<i> I'm Ricardo Jacinto.</i>

41
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:19,000
<i>The new owner
of Ginintuang Lupa!</i>

42
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:20,000
- [CROWD GASPS]
<i> - Yes!</i>

43
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,367
He wants to demolish our homes!

44
00:02:21,533 --> 00:02:22,767
- [ALL]<i> What?!
</i> - Ricardo!

45
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,000
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]
- [BLOW LANDS]

46
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,367
<i>You'll pay for what you did
to my family!</i>

47
00:02:26,533 --> 00:02:28,333
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [RICARDO SCREAMS]

48
00:02:28,433 --> 00:02:31,267
<i> I'll make sure that some day</i>

49
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,933
<i>I'll drive all of you
out of here!</i>

50
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:34,200
<i> We'll be back!</i>

51
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:36,100
- [PEOPLE CLAMMORING]
- [THUDDING]

52
00:02:36,233 --> 00:02:37,867
<i>We should report this
to the police!</i>

53
00:02:37,967 --> 00:02:40,733
<i>Your days are numbered here
in Ginintuang Lupa!</i>

54
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:44,167
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

55
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,700
You're so reckless!

56
00:02:45,867 --> 00:02:48,700
Are you a kid?
Throwing hands like that?

57
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,200
Who were you even fighting?!

58
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,733
He should be grateful
I didn't go all out!

59
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:55,067
What if he sued you, stupid!

60
00:02:55,233 --> 00:02:57,300
- I'm not afraid of him!
- That's right!

61
00:02:57,433 --> 00:03:01,233
We shouldn't let those bastards
intimidate us!

62
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:04,067
Even if they're powerful,
we won't back down!

63
00:03:04,233 --> 00:03:05,800
We'll put up a fight!

64
00:03:05,933 --> 00:03:08,767
Rudy, do you know who
the man you beat up is?

65
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:10,867
He's the landlord
of Ginintuang Lupa.

66
00:03:10,967 --> 00:03:13,867
Your recklessness could put us
in a tight spot.

67
00:03:14,133 --> 00:03:15,933
Rudy, everyone!

68
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:18,400
We won't let that happen,
won't we?!

69
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:25,233
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING] Never!
- That's right!

70
00:03:25,433 --> 00:03:29,733
Everyone, we should put up
barricades as early as now!

71
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:31,900
- To stop them from entering!
- That's enough.

72
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,900
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING] Let's go!
- Let's do it!

73
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,733
- Come on!
- Let's move!

74
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:40,100
[CLAMORING CONTINUES]

75
00:03:40,267 --> 00:03:42,167
- [GRIM MUSIC PLAYING
- [ENGINE REVVING]

76
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:44,967
[ISOBEL] Ugh! Oh my gosh!

77
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:47,500
I reek!

78
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:49,067
- [RICARDO EXHALES]
- [ISOBEL SIGHS]

79
00:03:49,167 --> 00:03:50,267
[ISOBEL BREATHES SHARPLY]

80
00:03:50,433 --> 00:03:52,800
What are we going to do
with the investors?!

81
00:03:52,967 --> 00:03:54,333
Will they ever get back to us?

82
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:57,533
[ISOBEL] This is such
a disgrace!

83
00:03:58,333 --> 00:03:59,500
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

84
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:04,700
<i>But if you find
where the treasure is,</i>

85
00:04:05,033 --> 00:04:06,300
<i> we'll split it.</i>

86
00:04:06,467 --> 00:04:08,433
I can count on you, right, Rudy?

87
00:04:08,533 --> 00:04:11,467
[YOUNG RUDY]<i> If we get lucky,
</i> we'd get millions from it!

88
00:04:11,567 --> 00:04:12,700
[YOUNG RICARDO]<i> We've been
</i> digging for weeks

89
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:13,800
<i> and still nothing!</i>

90
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,767
<i>The map said
it's located here, sir.</i>

91
00:04:15,867 --> 00:04:18,300
Are we really going to stop now
<i> when we're already so close</i>

92
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:20,000
<i> to finding the treasure?</i>

93
00:04:20,167 --> 00:04:22,467
<i>That's the problem with you.
That's what you always say!</i>

94
00:04:22,633 --> 00:04:25,033
<i>We're almost there,
it's always an almost!</i>

95
00:04:25,167 --> 00:04:26,633
<i> I'm getting sucked dry, Rudy!</i>

96
00:04:26,733 --> 00:04:28,467
<i> I shouldn't have believed you!</i>

97
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,900
<i> I thought you're brave.</i>

98
00:04:30,033 --> 00:04:31,800
Seems like that's not the case.
<i> Coward!</i>

99
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,800
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [YOUNG RUDY GRUNTING]

100
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:37,333
[THUDDING]

101
00:04:37,433 --> 00:04:38,533
[YOUNG RICARDO]
<i> The treasure doesn't exist.</i>

102
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:40,233
<i> He was just fantasizing it.</i>

103
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,867
<i> Sir, the treasure exists!</i>

104
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:44,333
<i>- No way!
- [OBJECTS CLATTERING]</i>

105
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:48,033
<i>He already ran away with it!
I told you not to trust him!</i>

106
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,467
<i> Find him.</i>

107
00:04:49,567 --> 00:04:51,833
<i> No matter what it takes.</i>

108
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:54,333
<i> Rudy, you bastard!</i>

109
00:04:54,433 --> 00:04:57,467
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

110
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:58,800
How are you?

111
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:00,667
I-- I'm fine, Isobel.

112
00:05:01,067 --> 00:05:05,567
[RICARDO BREATHING HEAVILY]

113
00:05:05,733 --> 00:05:07,067
Wait a minute.

114
00:05:08,267 --> 00:05:10,200
The man you were brawling
with earlier...

115
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:11,533
who is he?

116
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:14,500
Why does it seem like
you've known each other before?

117
00:05:15,567 --> 00:05:17,033
He's a nobody.

118
00:05:18,967 --> 00:05:20,567
What were you thinking?!

119
00:05:20,733 --> 00:05:21,900
I can't believe you!

120
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:23,867
Why did you punch that man?

121
00:05:23,967 --> 00:05:25,600
Things just got worse!

122
00:05:25,733 --> 00:05:26,733
He's a monster!

123
00:05:27,367 --> 00:05:28,933
Don't you know who he is?

124
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:32,333
He's a monster!
I could kill him!

125
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:33,867
Rudy, what's going on?

126
00:05:34,067 --> 00:05:35,633
- Rudy!
- Who was that man?!

127
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,033
[MAMENG] Rudy! Rudy!

128
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:42,400
- [RUDY GRUNTS]
- [OBJECTS CLATTER]

129
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,367
Who was that? Who was that man?!

130
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:47,267
What did he do to you?

131
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:49,433
Why are you so mad at him?

132
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:52,567
He's the reason
why I'm suffering now.

133
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,567
[RUDY] He ruined my life.

134
00:05:55,967 --> 00:05:58,633
The reason why Gabo
is going through all of this!

135
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:01,233
What are you saying?

136
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:06,467
He's the one who stole
all the treasure that I had!

137
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,233
He's the one who stole it!

138
00:06:09,667 --> 00:06:10,933
He did it!

139
00:06:12,667 --> 00:06:15,067
His name is Ricardo Jacinto!

140
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:20,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:06:20,967 --> 00:06:21,933
[MAX SIGHS]

142
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,133
- [ESTRELLA] Lieutenant?
- [MAX] Yes?

143
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,733
These are the suspects in
the riding-in-tandem incident

144
00:06:24,833 --> 00:06:26,000
that happened last night.

145
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:30,133
Alright, run their prints
through our records.

146
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:33,467
The Chief is already asking me
for an update on them, Estrella.

147
00:06:33,633 --> 00:06:35,567
We need to catch them already!

148
00:06:35,667 --> 00:06:37,100
- [SIGHS]
- Yes, ma'am.

149
00:06:37,267 --> 00:06:38,333
- Lieutenant?
- Yes?

150
00:06:38,467 --> 00:06:40,567
There's a report of a
disturbance at Ginintuang Lupa!

151
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:44,333
My dad is there!

152
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:46,033
Estrella, let's go!

153
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:49,767
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:50,933
Dad!

155
00:06:55,567 --> 00:06:56,767
[MAX] Dad?

156
00:06:57,733 --> 00:06:58,800
Dad?

157
00:06:59,367 --> 00:07:00,267
Are you okay?

158
00:07:00,367 --> 00:07:01,467
- What happened?
- Later, Max.

159
00:07:02,033 --> 00:07:03,800
[ISOBEL] I should've
gone with you!

160
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:05,633
- Ma? Are you okay?
- Oh my gosh!

161
00:07:05,733 --> 00:07:06,867
Goodness!

162
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,433
Look at what those scoundrels
from Ginintuang Lupa did!

163
00:07:10,133 --> 00:07:11,967
Where is your dad?
Let's go!

164
00:07:12,133 --> 00:07:13,967
- [ISOBEL] Let's go.
- You're so stubborn!

165
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:16,000
[MAX] You really had
to come along, Auntie Pinky!

166
00:07:19,867 --> 00:07:21,067
[RICARDO] Umali.

167
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:22,800
- Sir.
- Where's Domingo?

168
00:07:23,267 --> 00:07:24,533
He's in a meeting, sir.

169
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,667
[ROMULO] These criminals
have already escaped--

170
00:07:27,767 --> 00:07:28,833
[MAN] General.

171
00:07:28,933 --> 00:07:30,000
Sir!

172
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:33,633
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:07:33,733 --> 00:07:34,667
Dismissed.

174
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:41,733
- General Jacinto.
- Domingo.

175
00:07:41,867 --> 00:07:43,333
A court order has been issued

176
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,500
to remove all the squatters

177
00:07:45,933 --> 00:07:47,167
in Ginintuang Lupa!

178
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,200
But why are they still there?!

179
00:07:50,567 --> 00:07:52,700
Sir, this is a big operation.

180
00:07:53,233 --> 00:07:54,533
- We're gathering all the police

181
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,167
- by tomorrow--
- What do you mean by tomorrow?!

182
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:58,200
I want them out
of my land today!

183
00:07:58,867 --> 00:08:00,067
[ISOBEL] Oh my God!

184
00:08:00,567 --> 00:08:01,600
Sir!

185
00:08:02,467 --> 00:08:04,167
They're living on our land

186
00:08:04,267 --> 00:08:05,933
and look at what
they've done to us!

187
00:08:06,067 --> 00:08:08,200
We were treated like garbage!

188
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:11,067
Those people should've been gone
a long time ago!

189
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:13,000
Do whatever it takes
to remove them.

190
00:08:13,733 --> 00:08:15,033
Yes, General Jacinto.

191
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,867
I'll personally go to Ginintuang
Lupa and drive out

192
00:08:19,267 --> 00:08:21,667
those good-for-nothing
scoundrels who did this to you.

193
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,233
Santos.

194
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:26,733
Call my men.

195
00:08:26,833 --> 00:08:27,933
Yes, sir.

196
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:31,933
I promise you
that before this day ends,

197
00:08:32,833 --> 00:08:35,733
the people from Ginintuang Lupa
will be gone.

198
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:38,100
Colonel, permission
to join the operation, sir.

199
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,700
- No, no, no, no.
- Ma!

200
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,733
Just let them handle the work.

201
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:44,567
You stay here.

202
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:45,733
Max.

203
00:08:45,833 --> 00:08:47,233
Your mom is right.

204
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:49,733
Don't go, you're safer here
at the police station.

205
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:55,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:08:55,967 --> 00:08:57,233
Colonel.

207
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:02,167
Don't waste my trust.

208
00:09:04,167 --> 00:09:05,800
Yes, General Jacinto.

209
00:09:06,333 --> 00:09:07,600
[SIGHS]

210
00:09:08,667 --> 00:09:09,833
Hon.

211
00:09:10,767 --> 00:09:12,133
Let's go.

212
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,833
- I feel disgusting,
- [TWINKLE] Let's go.

213
00:09:14,967 --> 00:09:16,467
I need to shower!

214
00:09:16,633 --> 00:09:18,500
- Let's go.
- I need to wash this off!

215
00:09:18,633 --> 00:09:20,133
Sir, I'll see them out.

216
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,400
[ISOBEL] Did you see
what they've done?

217
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:28,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:09:28,833 --> 00:09:30,100
[SIGHS]

219
00:09:31,467 --> 00:09:32,600
Sir.

220
00:09:33,533 --> 00:09:36,300
We are earning a lot
from Ginintuang Lupa,

221
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,833
especially from Django.

222
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,467
Sir, what should we do?

223
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:41,267
It would be a waste
to lose that income.

224
00:09:41,367 --> 00:09:42,933
There is nothing we can do.

225
00:09:43,867 --> 00:09:46,800
General Jacinto's word is law.

226
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,267
If we don't follow his orders,

227
00:09:49,967 --> 00:09:51,300
we'll be the ones in trouble.

228
00:09:51,867 --> 00:09:52,967
[THUDS]

229
00:09:53,133 --> 00:09:58,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

230
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:06,767
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

231
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:09,467
- Max?
- [MAX] Hello, Sam?

232
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:11,133
I just saw Dad off
a few minutes ago.

233
00:10:11,533 --> 00:10:14,000
They were mobbed by the people
from Ginintuang Lupa

234
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,133
What?

235
00:10:15,367 --> 00:10:16,700
Wait a minute, how are they?

236
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,000
I'll just go to them.

237
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,167
No, they're fine.
They're on the way home now.

238
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:23,233
The problem is that the people

239
00:10:23,367 --> 00:10:25,200
from Ginintuang Lupa
won't leave.

240
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,333
See? I told you.

241
00:10:27,433 --> 00:10:29,500
The people there
are really stubborn.

242
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,833
I'll just check on dad.

243
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,300
Alright. Take care, Sam.

244
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:37,533
[LINE DISCONNECTS]

245
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:45,067
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

246
00:10:46,267 --> 00:10:47,533
[CAR DOOR CLOSES, OPENS]

247
00:10:48,067 --> 00:10:50,367
Gosh, I'm so tired!

248
00:10:50,533 --> 00:10:51,900
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

249
00:10:53,367 --> 00:10:54,400
[SIGHS]

250
00:10:54,567 --> 00:10:56,900
[TWINKLE GASPS] Ma'am! Sir!
Goodness!

251
00:10:57,067 --> 00:10:59,500
- What happened?
- Isn't it obvious?!

252
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,667
- Here, clean this!
- [RICARDO] Water.

253
00:11:01,767 --> 00:11:03,367
Disinfect everything!
Even the things inside!

254
00:11:04,233 --> 00:11:05,867
[NONONG] Oh, sweetie,
if only you saw what happened!

255
00:11:05,967 --> 00:11:07,400
- It was chaos!
- Ricardo says he needs water.

256
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:10,133
The people in Ginintuang Lupa
threw things at us!

257
00:11:10,267 --> 00:11:11,967
Well, it's Ginintuang Lupa,
what do you expect?

258
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:14,600
That place is notorious,
especially to outsiders.

259
00:11:14,767 --> 00:11:16,600
- We were not outsiders.
- What?

260
00:11:16,933 --> 00:11:18,300
I am the owner of the land.

261
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:23,700
Those leeches have some nerve!

262
00:11:24,133 --> 00:11:27,067
They just found land
that doesn't belong to them,

263
00:11:27,233 --> 00:11:31,600
put up houses,
called it their home,

264
00:11:31,767 --> 00:11:34,900
moved their family in, and even
claimed it as their own!

265
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,133
That's crazy, isn't it?

266
00:11:36,267 --> 00:11:37,267
The nerve!

267
00:11:37,433 --> 00:11:39,600
They've already taken advantage
of the land,

268
00:11:39,767 --> 00:11:41,633
haven't paid their dues,

269
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:45,133
and then when the owner finally
tries to reclaim the land

270
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:48,933
they squatted on, they have
the nerve to get mad!

271
00:11:49,867 --> 00:11:51,100
What's mine...

272
00:11:53,433 --> 00:11:54,800
is mine.

273
00:11:54,967 --> 00:11:59,100
If anyone dares to take
my property,

274
00:11:59,267 --> 00:12:00,900
there will be consequences.

275
00:12:03,333 --> 00:12:05,467
Life taught me to
protect what's mine...

276
00:12:07,533 --> 00:12:12,333
so I'll spare no
one from Ginintuang Lupa.

277
00:12:12,467 --> 00:12:19,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,733
I can't believe the residents of
Ginintuang Lupa did that to you!

279
00:12:24,733 --> 00:12:27,867
Thank goodness you made it
out of there alive!

280
00:12:27,867 --> 00:12:29,133
[SHRIEKS IN DISGUST]

281
00:12:29,967 --> 00:12:31,333
Eww! Yikes!

282
00:12:32,467 --> 00:12:35,033
Hey. Tell me, sweetie.

283
00:12:35,033 --> 00:12:37,933
Do you honestly think
they are bad people?

284
00:12:38,567 --> 00:12:40,667
You just up and sided
with Ma'am Isobel

285
00:12:40,667 --> 00:12:43,067
as if you didn't grow up poor.

286
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:46,167
Look, I'm just trying to
appease Ma'am Isobel's anger.

287
00:12:46,167 --> 00:12:49,333
Otherwise, she might
take it out on me.

288
00:12:50,267 --> 00:12:51,567
You know what?

289
00:12:51,567 --> 00:12:56,100
I didn't like what the residents
of Ginintuang Lupa did either.

290
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:59,200
But I get where
they're coming from.

291
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,500
I understand their situation.

292
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,700
But I also understand
our bosses.

293
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,033
Now, I don't know
which side to take.

294
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,100
Well, if...

295
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:12,600
If a property is being
underutilized,

296
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:15,533
why can't they just let
others make use of it?

297
00:13:15,533 --> 00:13:17,767
If they weren't gatekeeping it,

298
00:13:17,767 --> 00:13:19,967
they wouldn't have
this problem now!

299
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:22,567
Look at it this way.

300
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:27,433
Ma'am Isobel and Sir Ricardo
never experienced being poor.

301
00:13:27,433 --> 00:13:32,200
That's why they wouldn't
understand our plight.

302
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,967
I don't know
what to think anymore.

303
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:37,367
Are our bosses just selfish?

304
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:40,733
Or do rich people
just think like that?

305
00:13:41,867 --> 00:13:44,867
We can never know, right?

306
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:47,867
Exactly my point.

307
00:13:47,867 --> 00:13:48,933
Mm-hmm.

308
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:51,867
- [SIGHS]
- Let me help you with that.

309
00:13:51,867 --> 00:13:54,700
- [TWINKLE] So disgusting!
- [TOTO] If only you were there.

310
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,767
[PHONE BUZZING]

311
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:03,400
[LINE RINGING]

312
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:06,167
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

313
00:14:06,167 --> 00:14:07,933
Sam, what's the matter?

314
00:14:09,967 --> 00:14:12,100
Something happened
to my parents.

315
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:13,733
And they're not picking up.

316
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:14,967
Wait here.

317
00:14:14,967 --> 00:14:18,433
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:14:18,433 --> 00:14:20,167
- Sir.
- Yes?

319
00:14:20,167 --> 00:14:23,633
May I go home for a bit
to check on my parents?

320
00:14:23,633 --> 00:14:25,000
Why? Is there a problem?

321
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,733
My father went to check
their development project

322
00:14:26,733 --> 00:14:29,467
in Ginintuang Lupa,
but I heard a riot ensued.

323
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,267
I just want to check
if they're alright.

324
00:14:31,267 --> 00:14:33,767
Okay, go check
on your parents.

325
00:14:33,767 --> 00:14:35,500
Make sure they are okay.

326
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:39,600
If you have to be with them,
you can leave your post early.

327
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,000
Thank you, sir.

328
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,300
B-But don't worry.
I'll be back shortly.

329
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,533
Take care.

330
00:14:45,533 --> 00:14:48,167
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

331
00:14:48,167 --> 00:14:49,833
The place we've slated
for demolition

332
00:14:49,833 --> 00:14:52,600
is riddled with criminals
and murderers.

333
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,500
Show them no mercy.

334
00:14:55,500 --> 00:15:00,033
Men! It's our duty to
enforce the law! Let's move!

335
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:01,467
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

336
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:06,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

337
00:15:06,867 --> 00:15:09,500
Here's your phone, ma'am.
I already disinfected it.

338
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:12,800
I also cleaned your bag.
It's spotless now.

339
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:16,167
Sam called.

340
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,200
- [DOOR OPENS]
- Mom?

341
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,367
- Dad?
- [DOOR CLOSES]

342
00:15:22,667 --> 00:15:24,200
[SAM] How are you?

343
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,633
- You weren't picking up!
- [ISOBEL] Sam...

344
00:15:26,633 --> 00:15:28,133
I'm sorry, Sam.

345
00:15:28,133 --> 00:15:30,033
I had my phone disinfected
because--

346
00:15:30,033 --> 00:15:33,167
Why are you back so early?!
You should still be on duty.

347
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:35,933
I stepped out for a bit

348
00:15:35,933 --> 00:15:37,967
because I was worried
something had happened to you.

349
00:15:38,933 --> 00:15:41,067
Dad, why did you go there?

350
00:15:41,067 --> 00:15:43,633
Can't I go see Ginintuang Lupa?

351
00:15:44,567 --> 00:15:45,933
You know it's dangerous there.

352
00:15:45,933 --> 00:15:47,233
There's nothing wrong

353
00:15:47,233 --> 00:15:49,733
with me personally checking
on the land I own.

354
00:15:49,733 --> 00:15:52,533
Wait, Ricardo.
That's not what she means.

355
00:15:53,567 --> 00:15:55,333
Our daughter is just worried.

356
00:15:56,567 --> 00:15:59,433
Sam, you don't have to worry.

357
00:15:59,433 --> 00:16:01,367
We're alright. We're safe.

358
00:16:01,367 --> 00:16:03,733
Safe?
Mommy, you were mobbed!

359
00:16:03,733 --> 00:16:05,767
What if something else
had happened to you?

360
00:16:05,767 --> 00:16:08,000
You know, it's better if you
put the clearing operations

361
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,267
on hold for now.

362
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:10,700
I know what I'm doing

363
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,467
and what I should do
with my property!

364
00:16:12,467 --> 00:16:15,733
- Ricardo, that's enough.
- No, no! She's forgetting...

365
00:16:15,733 --> 00:16:17,767
...that I'm an ex-general!

366
00:16:17,767 --> 00:16:19,600
And I get things done!

367
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:23,400
I will not let anybody
tell me what to do!

368
00:16:25,433 --> 00:16:28,100
- Most especially you, Samantha.
- [ISOBEL] Oh my god.

369
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,600
Ricardo--
Ricardo, what did you just say?!

370
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,433
Ricardo, take that back. Hey!

371
00:16:34,433 --> 00:16:40,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

372
00:16:49,833 --> 00:16:51,100
[ISOBEL] Uh...

373
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:56,233
Sam...

374
00:16:59,667 --> 00:17:01,800
I'm sorry about your dad.

375
00:17:02,833 --> 00:17:04,633
He's still pissed off

376
00:17:04,633 --> 00:17:08,233
after what the residents of
Ginintuang Lupa did to us.

377
00:17:08,967 --> 00:17:10,467
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

378
00:17:10,467 --> 00:17:12,933
He hasn't calmed down.

379
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:17,100
But he didn't mean
what he said.

380
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:20,467
Mom...

381
00:17:21,367 --> 00:17:24,000
He meant it.
I know he did.

382
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:26,967
You don't have to defend Papa.

383
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:29,800
It's not like that.

384
00:17:30,533 --> 00:17:32,200
But...

385
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:35,700
I hope you don't hold it
against him.

386
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,400
Don't resent him.

387
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,167
That's not going to happen.

388
00:17:43,633 --> 00:17:46,333
That's why I'm doing
everything I can

389
00:17:46,333 --> 00:17:48,733
to prove to him
that I deserve his love.

390
00:17:50,333 --> 00:17:51,933
That I deserve his forgiveness.

391
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:55,133
Dear, your daddy loves you.

392
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,867
But people just have
different ways

393
00:17:58,867 --> 00:18:00,967
of showing affection.

394
00:18:00,967 --> 00:18:08,033
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

395
00:18:08,033 --> 00:18:10,200
We both know the truth, Mom.

396
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,567
Uh... [INHALES DEEPLY]

397
00:18:14,567 --> 00:18:17,300
I have to go back to work.

398
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:20,333
[SNIFFLES] I just made sure
you're safe.

399
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:28,667
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

400
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:37,500
[LINE RINGING]

401
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:40,100
Hello, Umali?
Why are you calling?

402
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:42,333
I was calling your father.

403
00:18:42,333 --> 00:18:45,100
But he's not answering.
I can't reach him.

404
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:49,667
- They're in Batangas for work.
- We have to meet.

405
00:18:49,667 --> 00:18:51,433
There's something important
we need to discuss

406
00:18:51,433 --> 00:18:53,267
[UMALI] about Ginintuang Lupa.

407
00:18:53,267 --> 00:18:54,633
Let's meet near the front.

408
00:18:55,633 --> 00:18:56,700
[LINE DROPS]

409
00:18:56,700 --> 00:19:00,767
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:19:00,767 --> 00:19:02,433
Call them.
We're going somewhere.

411
00:19:03,233 --> 00:19:04,233
Alright.

412
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,167
[GABO] Boss.

413
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:12,233
We'll get going.

414
00:19:14,233 --> 00:19:15,933
Boss...

415
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:18,100
If it's possible,
could we get our pay?

416
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:19,733
You just started working here,

417
00:19:19,733 --> 00:19:21,067
and now you're asking
for your pay?

418
00:19:21,933 --> 00:19:24,333
- You might stop working for me!
- No, boss.

419
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:29,433
Please, boss.
Even just our pay for today.

420
00:19:29,467 --> 00:19:30,900
Fine, 200 pesos.

421
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:34,833
Boss, that's too small.
Isn't our pay 600 pesos daily?

422
00:19:34,833 --> 00:19:38,567
No can do!
I can only give you 200 pesos!

423
00:19:38,567 --> 00:19:42,533
- Take it or leave it!
- Fine, that's okay.

424
00:19:45,967 --> 00:19:51,167
[BILLS RUSTLING]

425
00:19:51,167 --> 00:19:52,200
Here.

426
00:19:53,633 --> 00:19:55,433
[BILLS RUSTLING]

427
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,167
Hm.

428
00:19:59,167 --> 00:20:00,733
See, you caved in, anyway.

429
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:03,900
Make sure you come to work
early tomorrow.

430
00:20:03,933 --> 00:20:05,300
- Yes.
- Is that clear?

431
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,467
- Yes, boss.
- It's clear.

432
00:20:06,467 --> 00:20:08,500
We'll be here
very early tomorrow.

433
00:20:09,433 --> 00:20:10,933
Alright.

434
00:20:10,933 --> 00:20:14,133
We'll get going now.
We'll return tomorrow.

435
00:20:14,133 --> 00:20:15,767
Thank you, boss!

436
00:20:15,767 --> 00:20:17,100
- Thanks, boss!
- See you tomorrow.

437
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:21,267
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

438
00:20:21,267 --> 00:20:22,300
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

439
00:20:23,367 --> 00:20:24,433
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

440
00:20:26,467 --> 00:20:27,433
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

441
00:20:29,267 --> 00:20:30,267
[CLOTHES THUMP]

442
00:20:30,267 --> 00:20:33,267
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

443
00:20:33,267 --> 00:20:34,833
Hey! You!

444
00:20:34,833 --> 00:20:36,133
What are you doing?
Get inside!

445
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:37,967
[MAN] What?

446
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:39,700
Hurry up!

447
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:46,033
Django, Django, Django.

448
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:48,767
We're claiming Ginintuang Lupa.

449
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:50,767
We're going to demolish it.

450
00:20:51,633 --> 00:20:52,600
What?

451
00:20:53,533 --> 00:20:54,867
Why?

452
00:20:54,867 --> 00:20:58,833
When Ginintuang Lupa is gone,
you know we go out of business.

453
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:01,467
You'll lose money from that too!

454
00:21:01,467 --> 00:21:02,833
[UMALI CHUCKLING]

455
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,167
We know.

456
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:08,533
But this is an order
from the higher-ups.

457
00:21:09,433 --> 00:21:10,900
Our hands are tied.

458
00:21:12,367 --> 00:21:13,467
Umali...

459
00:21:15,667 --> 00:21:18,200
We won't accept losing
our livelihood.

460
00:21:20,333 --> 00:21:23,267
Hey. Don't forget
who you're talking to.

461
00:21:23,267 --> 00:21:27,567
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

462
00:21:27,567 --> 00:21:29,800
Remember, you're just this small
to me.

463
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:32,000
I can smash you to a pulp.

464
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:35,033
Want me to try it out?

465
00:21:37,833 --> 00:21:38,867
[GUN COCKS]

466
00:21:38,867 --> 00:21:43,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

467
00:21:43,367 --> 00:21:44,367
Put those down!

468
00:21:48,933 --> 00:21:49,933
Umali.

469
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,500
Remember this.

470
00:21:54,133 --> 00:21:56,333
It's not easy
to get Ginintuang Lupa.

471
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:59,600
The people there can kill.

472
00:22:00,433 --> 00:22:01,733
Remember that.

473
00:22:01,733 --> 00:22:02,833
[UMALI SCOFFS]

474
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:05,200
We'll see.

475
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:12,067
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

476
00:22:12,067 --> 00:22:14,267
Come on. I'm getting bored.

477
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:18,967
You? Why do you keep staring?!

478
00:22:19,733 --> 00:22:21,133
What did I do?

479
00:22:21,133 --> 00:22:23,633
[ELTON] Folks, keep this
in mind.

480
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:25,333
We have to be prepared
and stay alert.

481
00:22:25,333 --> 00:22:27,333
I'm sure those guys
will come back!

482
00:22:27,333 --> 00:22:29,967
Have our people made
a barricade?

483
00:22:29,967 --> 00:22:32,833
- Yes, it's done!
- And remember...

484
00:22:32,833 --> 00:22:36,767
We should never let them enter
Ginintuang Lupa!

485
00:22:36,767 --> 00:22:38,567
- This is our land!
- That's right!

486
00:22:38,567 --> 00:22:40,300
[NEIGHBOR] The police are here!
The police are here!

487
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:42,000
The police are here.
Let's get to the barricade!

488
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:44,333
- Come on!
- Let's get to the barricade!

489
00:22:44,333 --> 00:22:51,033
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

490
00:22:52,333 --> 00:22:55,633
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]
- [FIRETRUCK HORN BLARING]

491
00:22:56,967 --> 00:22:58,167
[FIRETRUCK HORN BLARING]

492
00:22:58,167 --> 00:22:59,167
[CAR HOOD THUDS]

493
00:22:59,167 --> 00:23:03,767
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

494
00:23:03,767 --> 00:23:05,267
[ELTON] Rudy. Rudy!

495
00:23:06,467 --> 00:23:07,633
Rudy!

496
00:23:08,133 --> 00:23:11,767
Rudy, the police are here.
They'll demolish our place!

497
00:23:12,433 --> 00:23:14,133
Wait. Rudy!

498
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:16,600
- What should we do? Rudy.
- Rudy.

499
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:18,600
- They can't do this.
- But...

500
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:19,600
[MAMENG STAMMERING]

501
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:20,933
- [BETCHAY] Wait!
- [MAMENG] Don't do it!

502
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:21,967
[ELTON] Rudy!

503
00:23:23,700 --> 00:23:25,967
The police are here!
Are you ready?!

504
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:27,300
We're ready!

505
00:23:27,300 --> 00:23:28,567
This is our land,

506
00:23:28,567 --> 00:23:31,467
and we won't let them take it
from us!

507
00:23:31,467 --> 00:23:33,000
- Is that right?!
- [NEIGHBORS] That's right!

508
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,033
Let's go!

509
00:23:34,033 --> 00:23:37,967
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

510
00:23:40,467 --> 00:23:41,967
[SMUG] Oh no, boss.

511
00:23:41,967 --> 00:23:45,100
I think Daboy, Binoy, and Tolits
are following us.

512
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,200
To take revenge?

513
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:52,500
- As if they can fight Gabo.
- [IPE] Those guys never learn.

514
00:23:54,300 --> 00:23:57,800
[TOLITS, BINOY] Stand up.
Stand up, stand up.

515
00:23:57,833 --> 00:23:59,633
What are you doing here? Huh?

516
00:24:00,933 --> 00:24:02,533
You'll take revenge?

517
00:24:02,533 --> 00:24:03,667
- Huh?!
- No, no, no.

518
00:24:03,667 --> 00:24:05,567
- That's not true!
- That's not true!

519
00:24:05,567 --> 00:24:09,500
Well, we're following you
because we want to talk to you.

520
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,500
Could we join your group?

521
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:14,933
Hey, what do you mean
join our group?

522
00:24:14,933 --> 00:24:17,367
Don't act like we're the same.
You're bad people!

523
00:24:17,367 --> 00:24:20,067
You never did anything good
for others!

524
00:24:20,067 --> 00:24:23,333
[TOLITS] We actually want
to turn over a new leaf.

525
00:24:23,333 --> 00:24:24,733
I've already heard that.

526
00:24:24,733 --> 00:24:27,333
[MAMMOTH] Gabo, we don't want
to be with Sir Paquito anymore.

527
00:24:27,333 --> 00:24:29,733
He keeps making us
do bad things.

528
00:24:29,767 --> 00:24:33,367
The truth is, we only rob others
to reach our quota.

529
00:24:33,367 --> 00:24:34,333
It's true!

530
00:24:35,067 --> 00:24:36,867
Maybe you can take us in.

531
00:24:36,867 --> 00:24:39,633
[BINOY] It's true, Gabo.
We want to change our ways.

532
00:24:39,633 --> 00:24:41,767
Besides, we know
you're the real deal

533
00:24:41,767 --> 00:24:43,400
- at Ginintuang Lupa.
- Yeah!

534
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:45,067
If we're on your side...

535
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:47,133
Sir Paquito can't do anything
to us.

536
00:24:47,133 --> 00:24:48,533
He's scared of you,
you know? Right?

537
00:24:48,533 --> 00:24:50,300
- Yeah, he is.
- Right? He's scared of Gabo.

538
00:24:50,300 --> 00:24:51,467
[IPE] Well, Gabo?

539
00:24:51,467 --> 00:24:52,933
Do you feel sorry
for these guys?

540
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:55,200
They might just play with us.

541
00:24:56,033 --> 00:24:57,000
Better yet...

542
00:24:58,367 --> 00:24:59,933
Just find another group.

543
00:25:01,367 --> 00:25:02,533
I don't need any of you.

544
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:05,967
Go on!

545
00:25:07,633 --> 00:25:10,333
